From: OpenWrt
Subject: [PATCH] uds_daemon: guard AWDL reference out of POSIX builds

`resolve_result_callback()` unconditionally references `req->resolve_awdl`
and `AWDLInterfaceID`, neither of which exist anywhere in this open-source
tree -- AWDL (Apple Wireless Direct Link) is a macOS/iOS-only proximity
networking feature with no POSIX/Linux equivalent, and its real
implementation lives in Apple's closed-source internal headers, not in
this distribution. `is_split_awdl_query` is only ever used as a boolean
parameter to two structured-logging calls (UDS_LOG_ANSWER_EVENT), not for
any functional control flow, so on POSIX it's simply always false.

Upstream-Status: Inactive-Upstream [POSIX-specific fix]

--- a/mDNSShared/uds_daemon.c
+++ b/mDNSShared/uds_daemon.c
@@ -3626,7 +3626,11 @@ mDNSlocal void resolve_result_callback(mDNS *const m, DNSQuestion *question, c
     request_state *const req = question->QuestionContext;
     const mDNSu32 name_hash = mDNS_DomainNameFNV1aHash(&question->qname);
     const mDNSBool isMDNSQuestion = mDNSOpaque16IsZero(question->TargetQID);
+#ifdef POSIX_BUILD
+    const mDNSBool is_split_awdl_query = mDNSfalse; // AWDL does not exist on POSIX
+#else
     const mDNSBool is_split_awdl_query = (req->resolve_awdl && question->InterfaceID == AWDLInterfaceID);
+#endif
     UDS_LOG_ANSWER_EVENT(isMDNSQuestion ? MDNS_LOG_CATEGORY_MDNS : MDNS_LOG_CATEGORY_DEFAULT, MDNS_LOG_DEFAULT,
